# Copy to ~/.config/swarph/peer-reply-drain-<peer>.env and replace every
# <ABSOLUTE_PATH> placeholder. systemd expands %h/%i in unit directives, NOT
# inside EnvironmentFile values; leaving specifiers here would pass them to the
# CLI literally. These directories are service-owned, never monitor state.
SWARPH_PEER_SPOOL_DIR=<ABSOLUTE_PATH_TO_PEER_SERVICE_SPOOL>
SWARPH_PEER_REPLY_OUTBOX_DIR=<ABSOLUTE_PATH_TO_PEER_REPLY_OUTBOX>
# Tailnet IP, not the MagicDNS name (commander 2026-08-21): the IP needs only
# tailscale up; the name needs MagicDNS + the right search domain + no local
# collision. NOTE (2026-08-25): that reasoning still holds for choosing WHICH
# address to set — but no address is SHIPPED any more, because the box this
# template named was retired and every install inherited a dead default.
# REQUIRED — no host is shipped. A baked-in address expires when that box is
# retired (card #578: this template shipped a machine that no longer exists).
# SWARPH_GATEWAY=http://<your-gateway-host>:8788
SWARPH_TOKEN_FILE=<ABSOLUTE_PATH_TO_PEER_TOKEN_FILE>
